### Fitting MG94 with double instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -3340.17, AIC-c =  6832.41 (75 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.8268
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.0438
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.177               |    62.922     |                                   |
|               0.985               |    18.714     |                                   |
|               3.836               |    18.363     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double and triple instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -3335.29, AIC-c =  6824.72 (76 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.8213
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.0067
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.1741
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon between synonymous codon islands =   0.1741
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.183               |    64.025     |                                   |
|               1.004               |    17.358     |                                   |
|               3.804               |    18.618     |                                   |


